    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31045" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶλαρ</span></b> , τό, used only
		in nom. and acc. sg., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covering,
				shelter, defence</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶ. νηῶν τε καὶ
				αὐτῶν</span>
			<i>shelter for</i> ship and crew, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.338
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύματος εἶ</span>.
				<i>fence against</i> the waves, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.257
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝέλϝαρ</span>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴλω</span>.)</div>
